# WebAwesome Component Library Guide

WebAwesome is a web component library that provides custom HTML elements with built-in styling and behavior. All components are prefixed with `wa-` and can be used in HTML, MDX, and TSX files.

## Core Architecture

### Component Structure
- **Custom Elements**: All components use `wa-` prefix (e.g., `wa-button`, `wa-card`, `wa-page`)
- **Slot-based**: Components use slots for content composition
- **Attribute-driven**: Behavior controlled via HTML attributes
- **CSS Design Tokens**: Consistent spacing, colors, and typography

### Common Attributes
Most components support these patterns:
- `variant`: Color scheme (`'brand' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'danger' | 'neutral'`)
- `appearance`: Visual style (`'filled' | 'outlined' | 'plain'`)
- `size`: Component size (`'small' | 'medium' | 'large'`)
- `disabled`: Disable interaction (`boolean`)

## Essential Components

### Layout & Structure
```html
<!-- Page wrapper with responsive navigation -->
<wa-page view="desktop" mobile-breakpoint="1180">
  <header slot="header">...</header>
  <div slot="navigation">...</div> 
  <main>...</main>
</wa-page>

<!-- Flexible content container -->
<wa-card appearance="outlined">
  <div slot="header">Card Title</div>
  <p>Card content</p>
  <div slot="footer">Actions</div>
</wa-card>
```

### Interactive Elements
```html
<!-- Buttons with variants and states -->
<wa-button variant="brand" appearance="filled" size="medium">
  <wa-icon slot="start" name="plus"></wa-icon>
  Add Item
</wa-button>

<!-- Form controls -->
<wa-input label="Email" type="email" placeholder="user@example.com" required></wa-input>
<wa-checkbox checked>Enable notifications</wa-checkbox>
<wa-select placeholder="Choose option">
  <wa-option value="1">Option 1</wa-option>
  <wa-option value="2">Option 2</wa-option>
</wa-select>
```

### Content & Display
```html
<!-- Icons with semantic labels -->
<wa-icon name="envelope" label="Send email"></wa-icon>

<!-- User representations -->
<wa-avatar image="/user.jpg" label="John Doe" shape="circle"></wa-avatar>
<wa-avatar initials="JD" label="John Doe"></wa-avatar>

<!-- Status indicators -->
<wa-badge variant="success" pill>Online</wa-badge>
<wa-callout variant="warning">Important notice</wa-callout>
```

### Navigation & Organization
```html
<!-- Tabbed interfaces -->
<wa-tab-group>
  <wa-tab panel="tab1">Overview</wa-tab>
  <wa-tab panel="tab2">Details</wa-tab>
  <wa-tab-panel name="tab1">Overview content</wa-tab-panel>
  <wa-tab-panel name="tab2">Details content</wa-tab-panel>
</wa-tab-group>

<!-- Breadcrumb navigation -->
<wa-breadcrumb>
  <wa-breadcrumb-item href="/">Home</wa-breadcrumb-item>
  <wa-breadcrumb-item href="/products">Products</wa-breadcrumb-item>
  <wa-breadcrumb-item>Current Page</wa-breadcrumb-item>
</wa-breadcrumb>
```

## Layout Utilities

### CSS Classes for Layout
- **Stacking**: `wa-stack` (vertical), `wa-cluster` (horizontal)
- **Alignment**: `wa-split` (space-between), `wa-flank` (start-aligned with gap)
- **Spacing**: `wa-gap-xs`, `wa-gap-s`, `wa-gap-m`, `wa-gap-l`, `wa-gap-xl`
- **Grid**: `wa-grid` with `--min-column-size` CSS custom property
- **Flex**: `wa-flex`, `wa-align-items-center`, `wa-justify-content-between`

### Spacing Examples
```html
<!-- Vertical stack with medium gap -->
<div class="wa-stack wa-gap-m">
  <wa-card>First item</wa-card>
  <wa-card>Second item</wa-card>
</div>

<!-- Responsive grid -->
<div class="wa-grid wa-gap-m" style="--min-column-size: 200px;">
  <wa-card>Grid item 1</wa-card>
  <wa-card>Grid item 2</wa-card>
  <wa-card>Grid item 3</wa-card>
</div>
```

## Common Patterns

### Dashboard Cards
```html
<wa-card>
  <div class="wa-stack wa-gap-xs">
    <span class="wa-caption-m">Metric Label</span>
    <span class="wa-heading-2xl">$24,560</span>
    <span class="wa-caption-s wa-success">+8% this month</span>
  </div>
</wa-card>
```

### Action Bars
```html
<div class="wa-split">
  <h2>Page Title</h2>
  <div class="wa-cluster">
    <wa-button appearance="outlined">Cancel</wa-button>
    <wa-button variant="brand">Save</wa-button>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Loading States
```html
<wa-button loading disabled>Processing...</wa-button>
<wa-spinner></wa-spinner>
<wa-skeleton effect="pulse"></wa-skeleton>
```

### Dialogs & Overlays
```html
<wa-dialog label="Confirm Action" open>
  <p>Are you sure you want to delete this item?</p>
  <div slot="footer" class="wa-cluster">
    <wa-button appearance="outlined">Cancel</wa-button>
    <wa-button variant="danger">Delete</wa-button>
  </div>
</wa-dialog>
```

## Typography & Design Tokens

### Text Styles
- Headings: `wa-heading-xs` through `wa-heading-3xl`
- Body: `wa-body-s`, `wa-body-m`, `wa-body-l`
- Captions: `wa-caption-xs`, `wa-caption-s`, `wa-caption-m`

### Color Utilities
- Semantic: `wa-success`, `wa-warning`, `wa-danger`, `wa-neutral`
- Use with text, backgrounds, and borders

## Best Practices

1. **Always provide labels** for icons and interactive elements
2. **Use semantic variants** (`success`, `danger`) over generic styling
3. **Leverage slots** for flexible content composition
4. **Combine layout classes** for responsive designs
5. **Use design tokens** (`var(--wa-space-m)`) for consistent spacing
6. **Follow accessibility patterns** built into components

## TypeScript Support

For TSX files, WebAwesome components are fully typed with:
- Attribute IntelliSense
- Event handler typing
- Slot content validation
- Custom property support

Example in TSX:
```tsx
<wa-button 
  variant="brand" 
  onClick={(e) => handleClick(e)}
  disabled={isLoading}
>
  <wa-icon slot="start" name="plus" />
  Add Item
</wa-button>
```

This component system emphasizes composition over configuration - build complex UIs by combining simple, purpose-built components with consistent design tokens.
